# drivers/gpu/conf: the GPU.
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_<NAME>=y in a defconfig builds a driver into the kernel; "standard" files are always built.
# tools/hakios-config.py reads this file; docs/drivers-config.md says what each word means and how it reaches XNU.

driver ADRENO
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.adreno.c
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.adreno.sdm845.c
	file    iokit/Kernel/hakios.gpu.cpp iokitcpp
	help    Redwood Adreno 642L and Polaris Adreno 630 backends with the shared HakiosGPU service. On Polaris, gpu=1
	help    runs guarded A630 startup and starts HakiosGPU only after the adreno=23 client-root IB and kernel-root
	help    fence pass; adreno=1..23 selects diagnostic stages without starting the service.
	help    Diagnostic stages: read-only GPU probes (adreno=1..6), explicit PAS ZAP staging (adreno=7), RPMh discovery (adreno=8),
	help    detached HFI memory preparation (adreno=9), reset-held GMU ITCM loading (adreno=10),
	help    GMU-kernel SID5 attach (adreno=11), GMU/HFI startup (adreno=12), PERF_TBL (adreno=13),
	help    PERF_TBL/BW_VOTE_TBL submission (adreno=14), offline CP packet construction (adreno=15),
	help    detached CP buffer preparation (adreno=16), guarded GX startup (adreno=17), core setup
	help    (adreno=18), ZAP authentication and CP_ME_INIT (adreno=19), unsecured CP mode (adreno=20),
	help    kernel-owned fence (adreno=21), CPU-driven root switch (adreno=22), and client-root memory-write probe
	help    (adreno=23). Polaris write stages are unverified on hardware; asynchronous scheduling, hang recovery, DVFS,
	help    and orderly GPU shutdown still need implementation and validation. gpu=1 is an explicit opt-in.
	help    Both devices need their own firmware in fw-gpu/.
